<title>GERMANY: SOCCER-RUFER REUNITED WITH REHHAGEL.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-RUFER REUNITED WITH REHHAGEL.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German second division leaders Kaiserslautern have signed New Zealand striker Wynton Rufer, reuniting him with Otto Rehhagel, his coach for six years at Werder Bremen, the club said on Monday.</p>
<p>Rufer, 34, helped steer Bremen to the 1993 championship under Rehhagel and since 1995 has been playing for JEF United Ichihara in Japan.</p>
<p>He could yet play in the top flight again as Kaiserslautern look set to rebound into the first division at the first attempt.</p>
</text>
